{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us","id":531146,"title":"Collectors among us","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-28T11:13:13-07:00","id":531146,"title":"Collectors among us","content":"A vain post, but one I can't resist putting out there. Are there any other collectors of the out-of-print books here? I somewhat hesitantly pride myself on a few finds over the years and I was wondering: what books do you find are particularly elusive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:18:40-07:00","id":531156,"title":"","content":"<b>Shadow Player's Guide</b> for Wraith took me <i>forever </i>to find!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:26:32-07:00","id":531163,"title":"","content":"Ravenloft Carnivale. Found that mint in the back of a old store for 4 Euros :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:14:43-07:00","id":531404,"title":"","content":"I used to have all the books for VtM, and most of the books for WtA and MtA. I lost all of them back in 2006. In the VtM line I even had a copy of the Player's Guide to the Sabbat that was a miss print with a white cover and blue lettering. Now most of my books are in PDF format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:51:13-07:00","id":531457,"title":"","content":"I grabbed a couple extra copies of the W20 HME (partly just to make sure they got made). Does that count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:08:15-07:00","id":531529,"title":"","content":"Well, I picked up Street Fighter, the SF player's guide, and SF storyteller's screen. I have almost all the WWGS produced Vampire, Werewolf, and Wraith books, and all the Black Dog ones. (Charnel Houses of Europe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T22:08:44-07:00","id":531733,"title":"","content":"I paid $90 for <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres </i>when it was out of print, and then picked up another copy when White Wolf finally reprinted it years later. So I have the glossy black cover and the matte black one as well. Of course, now you can buy the PDF for peanuts...<br /> <br /> I also have the limited edition versions of all the Revised books that were published. And the limited edition hardcover of the Book of Nod that came with the deluxe edition of the <i>Redemption </i>game (along with the necklace).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 05-29-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T23:10:10-07:00","id":531750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us?p=531163#post531163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravenloft Carnivale. Found that mint in the back of a old store for 4 Euros :P</div> </div> </div> </div>You bastard... I'd love a copy of that. Ravenloft and I go back to Day One when it was printed in '83. I had already been running it as a setting/&quot;reality&quot; for several years when the first black box setting came out in '90. Hell, coincidentally enough, I am staring at a stack of old Ravenloft models/books over in the corner that I (eventually) have to re-sort into new tubs for storage. (I have at least 3 copies of the original module -- math/architectural errors on the castle's height and all -- as well as this, that and the other from over the years... but not Carnivale... at least not in a solid form....) <br /> <br /> A couple friends let out the &quot;geek gasp&quot; when I happened to take out the original black-box map of The Core, pre-Azalin blowing Markovia out into the middle of the &quot;sea&quot;. It's one thing to have all of whatever crap on the computer, but something else entirely to have the physical item (book, map, module, what-have-you) in hand or on a table. It's just a completely different thing....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:25:10-07:00","id":531772,"title":"","content":"Having missed the Kickstarter, Children of the Revolution Deluxe took me a long time to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T09:48:41-07:00","id":532019,"title":"","content":"The Italian version of Clanbook Cappadocian &amp; Costantinoples by Night are quite prized...<br /> they were around 30 \u20ac back when they were disponible... now more...<br /> <br /> and I got both","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T12:02:40-07:00","id":534671,"title":"","content":"I've held on to all of my RPG purchases for the last 25 years. I actually wanted to pledge to a higher reward tier in the Wraith 20 kickstarter, but I already had physical copies of all the books they were offering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:50:46-07:00","id":535532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us?p=531733#post531733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dark Reflections: Spectres </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Crap, forgot about that one. Still haven't secured a copy. The <i>only </i>Wraith book I'm missing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:56:06-07:00","id":535716,"title":"","content":"It took me years to find the Revised Tribebooks for Silent Striders, Fianna, and Children of Gaia. I lucked into 2 copies of TB:SS visiting a comic book shop after a horrid interview several years back. I sold one for $50. I could not for the life of me figure out why it took 10 years to get TB:CoG Revised when almost nobody likes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:28:25-07:00","id":542275,"title":"","content":"I'm something of a collector, but these days I travel overseas. I'm currently in China, but I'll be returning to the States in late July / early August. When I do, I'll be selling most of my hardcopy collection. I plan on putting an ad on the forums before I do, but if anyone wants to shoot me a list of needed books I'm happy to talk prices or trades (I can't sell hard my only hard copy until I have a PDF copy).<br /> <br /> That said, I have all the Dark Ages line, most of the VTM line (my ex-wife destroyed one of my books :/ ), and, frankly, pretty much all the other lines as well. Papa Bear, I have two copies of <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres</i>. If anyone is interested, shoot me a PM.<br /> <br /> Total aside, I've been trying to find any of the cWoD books in Chinese... were there never any printed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:22:55-07:00","id":547139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us?p=531733#post531733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I paid $90 for <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres </i>when it was out of print, and then picked up another copy when White Wolf finally reprinted it years later. So I have the glossy black cover and the matte black one as well. Of course, now you can buy the PDF for peanuts...<br /> <br /> I also have the limited edition versions of all the Revised books that were published. And the limited edition hardcover of the Book of Nod that came with the deluxe edition of the <i>Redemption </i>game (along with the necklace).<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>So is the matte one the reprint? That's the one I have. Gorgeous book (except <i>that</i> picture, if you know which one I mean). It was always highly sought after, and for good reason.<br /> <br /> I remember <i>The Risen</i> being hard to get hold of for ages too.<br /> <br /> I always try to buy the old books where I can, rather than ordering the PoD versions, because I'm a total print snob and don't like the print quality of Lightning Source. Onyx Path could use so many better PoD printers and the quality would be far superior. It's just a pity, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T12:08:47-07:00","id":547390,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't remember which is which, though I'm tempted to say the matte black cover is the original.<br /> <br /> And it's not really Onyx Path's choice on the PoD stuff - they just go through Drivethrurpg (who has an active participant in these forums - can't recall who - but he can most likely answer your concerns regarding PoD quality).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:56:02-07:00","id":547485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us?p=547390#post547390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly can't remember which is which, though I'm tempted to say the matte black cover is the original.<br /> <br /> And it's not really Onyx Path's choice on the PoD stuff - they just go through Drivethrurpg (who has an active participant in these forums - can't recall who - but he can most likely answer your concerns regarding PoD quality).<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understand that, and Drivethrurpg is relatively simple for them, but I'm sure other POD companies would provide higher quality at lower prices. I publish books using POD all the time, and Lightning Source (which does the OPP ones) is one of the worst. The paper quality and everything is just generally lower and their matte lamination covers feel really tacky to the touch.<br /> <br /> But, as I say, I'm a book snob :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:48:24-07:00","id":548091,"title":"","content":"I have a matte-covered edition of Infernalism: Path of Screams, and I recall it being the first White Wolf book I found with the Arthaus imprint. Is this a similar reprint situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:28:25-07:00","id":565381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/531146-collectors-among-us?p=531404#post531404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to have all the books for VtM, and most of the books for WtA and MtA. I lost all of them back in 2006. In the VtM line I even had a copy of the Player's Guide to the Sabbat that was a miss print with a white cover and blue lettering. Now most of my books are in PDF format.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you, I lost all my WW books, though it was all the way back in 1998. Thanks to obsessive diligence and a nearby game store with an AMAZING used books section (thank you, Game Empire in Pasadena!), I've been able to assemble just about every OWoD publication in hardcopy. Kithbook: Pookas was tough to find, as were Secrets of Shadoloo and Infernalism: Path of Screams.<br /> <br /> My remaining pursuit is to chase down as many of the Art/Realm/Bunk cards from 1st Ed. Changeling: The Dreaming's forgotten CCG element as possible. Having players draw Bunks randomly from a deck of Bunks that corresponded to their Arts added a whimsical element that was uniquely C:tD, and with the bonus success for drawing, say, a Wayfare Bunk for a Wayfare Art, gave Arts dangerous potential. Eliminating Bunk dithering was a huge bonus as well.<br /> <br /> My biggest collecting regret was back in 2000 or so, when someone I knew sold off a bunch of collectibles to fund his wedding. He wanted to sell me his Werewolf: the Apocalypse Klaive for just $100, but I. Just. Could. Not. Spare. The. Money.<br /> <br /> Haunts me to this very day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:00:42-07:00","id":565820,"title":"","content":"I love being a collector, though most my rare books I bought new....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T18:57:45-07:00","id":565961,"title":"","content":"I have all of Wraith and Changeling, plus all the Vampire Revised and Mage Revised books and a few Second Edition ones in the original printings. I seem to find these turn up on ebay every now and again. The prices are pretty much the same as DriveThruRPG if you look around.<br /> <br /> I want to find a copy of V20 that isn't POD, but I doubt I'll get one for less than \u00a3100, which is too much for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}